//a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1653.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17435,"officials":[{"fullName":"Travis Gawryletz","displayName":"Travis Gawryletz","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jonny Murray","displayName":"Jonny Murray","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kyle Rehman","displayName":"Kyle Rehman","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Carter Sandlak","displayName":"Carter Sandlak","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Penguins beat Sharks 3-2 in shootout after blowing 2-goal lead in 3rd period","description":"— Ben Kindel scored in regulation and had the lone shootout goal and the Pittsburgh Penguins beat the San Jose Sharks 3-2 on Wednesday night after blowing a two-goal lead in third period.","story":"SAN JOSE, Calif. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5291947/ben-kindel\">Ben Kindel</a> scored in regulation and had the lone shootout goal and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-penguins\">Pittsburgh Penguins</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sj/san-jose-sharks\">San Jose Sharks</a> 3-2 on Wednesday night after blowing a two-goal lead in third period.\n\n\r\n              San Jose star <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5206628/macklin-celebrini\">Macklin Celebrini</a> scored with 8:28 left, and set up Mason Marchment’s tying goal with 4:11 remaining.\n\n\r\n              The Penguins then survived a San Jose power play for the final 43 seconds of overtime after <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3539/kris-letang\">Kris Letang</a> was sent off for holding <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5216880/sam-dickinson\">Sam Dickinson</a>'s stick.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188366/sergei-murashov\">Sergei Murashov</a> made 34 saves for the Penguins through overtime, then ended the tiebreaker by stopping <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149155/will-smith\">Will Smith</a> in the third round. Kindel scored on the first attempt of the shootout.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4063401/samuel-girard\">Samuel Girard</a> opened the scoring for Pittsburgh on a slap shot at 8:57 of the first period, and Kindel connected on a power play at 3:28 of the third.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697394/yaroslav-askarov\">Yaroslav Askarov</a> stopped 33 shots for San Jose.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Penguins: Host Ottawa on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              Sharks: At Utah on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-12T06:14:37Z"}}